# You design and build LEGO Technic models one step at a time, in a build language.
# 
# For each step you write:
# ADD name partnumber color
# CONNECT part.point -> part.point LOCKED|TURNS|STIFF   (points: hole1.., axlehole1.., pin1.., axle1.., clip1..; LOCKED = cross in cross, turn together; TURNS = free; STIFF = friction pin)
# Optional: MESH a.teeth b.teeth / RATIO a b x/y / GROUP g (opens a side build) / END (closes it) / ATTACH g (joins a finished side build into the main model)
# WHY one plain sentence: what this step builds and what it is for.
# A point ending in ~ is an estimate; ? means not known.
# 
# Rules: only use real points of each part; a round pin never goes in a cross hole; a shaft that must turn needs round holes; a worm needs stops on both sides; gears must sit at the right distance.
STEP 1
ADD p32278-1 32278 black
ADD p6558-1 6558 blue
ADD p6558-2 6558 blue
ADD p6558-3 6558 blue
ADD p6558-4 6558 blue
CONNECT p6558-1.pin1 -> p32278-1.hole15 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-2.pin1 -> p32278-1.hole12 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-3.pin1 -> p32278-1.hole1 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-4.pin1 -> p32278-1.hole4 STIFF
WHY Starts the tracked base with four long blue pins spaced three holes apart near the ends of the black fifteen-hole crossbeam.
STEP 2
ADD p32524-1 32524 lightgray
ADD p32524-2 32524 lightgray
CONNECT p6558-1.pin2 -> p32524-1.hole5 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-2.pin2 -> p32524-1.hole2 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-3.pin2 -> p32524-2.hole3 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-4.pin2 -> p32524-2.hole6 STIFF
WHY Fits a grey seven-hole beam across each blue pin pair with its outer end projecting beyond the crossbeam.
STEP 3
ADD p32526-1 32526 lightgray
ADD p32526-2 32526 lightgray
CONNECT p6558-1.pin3 -> p32526-2.hole2 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-2.pin3 -> p32526-2.hole5 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-3.pin3 -> p32526-1.hole2 STIFF
CONNECT p6558-4.pin3 -> p32526-1.hole5 STIFF
WHY Adds the two grey L beams on the remaining blue pin ends with their short legs pointing upward.
STEP 4
ADD p60485-1 60485 lightgray
ADD p60485-2 60485 lightgray
